Subject: [PATCH] instance: do not leave goroutines blocked after Start returns

StartWithPaths races two goroutines (the hostagent's events and its exit)
on unbuffered channels and returns on the first. The loser blocks on its
send for as long as the program lives: one goroutine per start in a program
that outlives the call (limactl exits, so it does not show there). The
channels hold one value, so the sends complete; the exit goroutine also
finishes its Wait, which reaps the hostagent when it ends.

No test: StartWithPaths starts a hostagent, which Lima's unit tests do not.

---
diff --git a/pkg/instance/start.go b/pkg/instance/start.go
index 0c70232a..489df5f9 100644
--- a/pkg/instance/start.go
+++ b/pkg/instance/start.go
@@ -319,12 +319,15 @@ func StartWithPaths(ctx context.Context, inst *limatype.Instance, launchHostAgen
 		return err
 	}
 
-	watchErrCh := make(chan error)
+	// Buffered: the goroutine that loses the race below must not block on its
+	// send for as long as the program lives (it would, once StartWithPaths
+	// has returned).
+	watchErrCh := make(chan error, 1)
 	go func() {
 		watchErrCh <- watchHostAgentEvents(ctx, inst, haStdoutPath, haStderrPath, begin, showProgress)
 		close(watchErrCh)
 	}()
-	waitErrCh := make(chan error)
+	waitErrCh := make(chan error, 1)
 	if haCmd != nil {
 		go func() {
 			waitErrCh <- haCmd.Wait()
